% Childcare support: a program written in Logical English and exported to DMN
% (File > Export to Another System > DMN). It uses what the DMN writer turns
% into DMN: values and conditions of one applicant (each applicant becomes a
% case of the DMN model), a decision table with first match, arithmetic, a
% list and its count, and scenarios that become the model's test cases
% (lpsPlus migration/dmn/dmn_roundtrip.pl runs them on Drools).

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the household income of *an applicant* is *an amount*.
    the number of adults of *an applicant* is *a number*.
    the children of *an applicant* include *a name*.
    *an applicant* works or studies.
    the income band of *an applicant* is *a band*.
    the band for an income per adult of *an amount* is *a band* under table income_bands.
    the number of children of *an applicant* is *a number*.
    the support rate of *an applicant* is *a rate*.
    the monthly support of *an applicant* is *an amount*.
    *an applicant* is eligible for childcare support.

the table income_bands is, with first match:
    income per adult | band
    <= 15000         | low
    <= 40000         | middle
    any              | high

the knowledge base childcare support includes:

the number of children of an applicant is a number N if
    the household income of the applicant is an amount
    and N is the count of each name such that
        the children of the applicant include the name.

an applicant is eligible for childcare support if
    the applicant works or studies
    and the number of children of the applicant is a number
    and the number > 0.

the income band of an applicant is a band if
    the household income of the applicant is an amount
    and the number of adults of the applicant is a number
    and the number > 0
    and P = the amount / the number
    and the band for an income per adult of P is the band under table income_bands.

the support rate of an applicant is 300 if
    the income band of the applicant is low.

the support rate of an applicant is 150 if
    the income band of the applicant is middle.

the support rate of an applicant is 0 if
    the income band of the applicant is high.

the monthly support of an applicant is an amount A if
    the applicant is eligible for childcare support
    and the support rate of the applicant is a rate R
    and the number of children of the applicant is a number N
    and A = R * N.

scenario two_families is:
    ana works or studies.
    the household income of ana is 24000.
    the number of adults of ana is 2.
    the children of ana include "Rita".
    the children of ana include "Tom".
    the household income of ben is 90000.
    the number of adults of ben is 1.
    the children of ben include "Lia".
    eligible expects answers ["ana is eligible for childcare support"].
    support expects answers ["the monthly support of ana is 600"].
    band expects answers ["the income band of ana is low", "the income band of ben is high"].

scenario single_parent is:
    carla works or studies.
    the household income of carla is 30000.
    the number of adults of carla is 1.
    the children of carla include "Noa".
    support expects answers ["the monthly support of carla is 150"].
    band expects answers ["the income band of carla is middle"].

query eligible is:
    which applicant is eligible for childcare support.

query support is:
    the monthly support of which applicant is which amount.

query band is:
    the income band of which applicant is which band.
